        "AbstractText": {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE PRESENTATION",
          "content": "A woman in her 50s with no significant medical history presented with low-grade fever and cough of 3 days' duration, which was productive of blood-streaked sputum. She was an active smoker, with a 30 pack-year history of smoking. She denied chest pain, chronic cough, exertional dyspnea, or constitutional symptoms."
        }
